x;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126097981.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-a-first-elon-musks-net-worth-tops-700-billion-heres-how-the-tech-titan-did-it/articleshow/126097981.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-a-first-elon-musks-net-worth-tops-700-billion-heres-how-the-tech-titan-did-it/articleshow/126097981.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2025-12-21T01:17:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126097981,imgsize-809453.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[$50 for $100? How this Indian-origin executive negotiated with a knife-wielding mugger on his first day in US]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126097163.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[When Sharran Srivatsaa, an 18-year-old Indian immigrant, landed in America, he was met with an unexpected challenge: a mugger brandishing a knife. Rather than panic, he tapped into his negotiation skills, proposing to hand over $100 in exchange for a safe passage to school with $50 still in his pocket.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/etimes/trending/50-for-100-how-this-indian-origin-executive-negotiated-with-a-knife-wielding-mugger-on-his-first-day-in-us/articleshow/126097163.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/etimes/trending/50-for-100-how-this-indian-origin-executive-negotiated-with-a-knife-wielding-mugger-on-his-first-day-in-us/articleshow/126097163.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2025-12-21T00:35:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Trending Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126097163,imgsize-427832.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Captain Puffy reveals Pokimane spoke to her about Ellum allegations before viral TikTok backlash began]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126097167.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Twitch streamer Cara, known as Captain Puffy, claims Pokimane was aware of serious allegations against Josh "Ellum" months before he moved in with her.  Captain Puffy stated she spoke with Pokimane in October 2025, detailing Ellum's alleged misconduct. Pokimane had previously commented on TikTok, saying she spoke to those involved, but Captain Puffy insists the conversation happened much earlier.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/captain-puffy-reveals-pokimane-spoke-to-her-about-ellum-allegations-before-viral-tiktok-backlash-began/articleshow/126097167.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/captain-puffy-reveals-pokimane-spoke-to-her-about-ellum-allegations-before-viral-tiktok-backlash-began/articleshow/126097167.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2025-12-20T23:55:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sehjal Gupta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126097173,imgsize-821972.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[“Envious of Charlie Kirk”: Candace Owens fires back at Ben Shapiro as AmFest clash shakes conservative media]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126096896.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Candace Owens and Ben Shapiro are locked in a public fight after Shapiro criticized her at AmFest. Owens fired back with sharp quotes on X and her podcast, making serious claims about Shapiro, Charlie Kirk, and The Daily Wire. Steve Bannon and Megyn Kelly also entered the debate, deepening the split in conservative media.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/envious-of-charlie-kirk-candace-owens-fires-back-at-ben-shapiro-as-amfest-clash-shakes-conservative-media/articleshow/126096896.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/envious-of-charlie-kirk-candace-owens-fires-back-at-ben-shapiro-as-amfest-clash-shakes-conservative-media/articleshow/126096896.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2025-12-20T23:39:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sehjal Gupta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126096879,imgsize-704950.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Gave money because I loved…’: Indian national Gagandeep Pejatta with 'intellectual disability' alleges $1 million exploitation by Canadian family, real estate broker]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126096300.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/gave-money-because-i-loved-indian-national-gagandeep-pejatta-alleges-1-million-exploitation-by-canadian-family-real-estate-broker/articleshow/126096300.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/gave-money-because-i-loved-indian-national-gagandeep-pejatta-alleges-1-million-exploitation-by-canadian-family-real-estate-broker/articleshow/126096300.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2025-12-20T23:47:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126096300,imgsize-517214.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Epstein files opened: Woman reported Jeffrey's interest in 'child pornography' to FBI in 1996; recalled seeing Trump at NY office]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126096016.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A woman's 1996 FBI complaint about Jeffrey Epstein's interest in child pornography, detailing alleged theft of her sisters' photos, was never publicly acknowledged. Maria Farmer claims federal investigators ignored her warnings for decades, only acting much later. Her testimony, now supported by an FBI report, highlights potential missed opportunities to stop Epstein's abuse sooner.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/epstein-files-opened-woman-reported-jeffreys-interest-in-child-pornography-to-fbi-in-1996-recalled-seeing-trump-at-ny-office/articleshow/126096016.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/epstein-files-opened-woman-reported-jeffreys-interest-in-child-pornography-to-fbi-in-1996-recalled-seeing-trump-at-ny-office/articleshow/126096016.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2025-12-20T22:45:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126096018,imgsize-1168469.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How Canada’s Indian Act tax rules are confusing shoppers: 'Indigenous people should be proud to get tax exemption']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126095589.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/how-canadas-indian-act-tax-rules-are-confusing-shoppers-indigenous-people-should-be-proud-to-get-tax-exemption/articleshow/126095589.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/how-canadas-indian-act-tax-rules-are-confusing-shoppers-indigenous-people-should-be-proud-to-get-tax-exemption/articleshow/126095589.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2025-12-20T22:42:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126095589,imgsize-1257145.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Request accepted: Egypt lifts travel ban on activist; played key role in 2011 uprising]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126095771.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Egypt's attorney general lifted a travel ban on prominent Egyptian-on Saturday, following a request submitted on his behalf. Despite the pardon, the Egyptian authorities stopped Abdel Fattah from travelling at Cairo airport last month as he prepared to fly to Britain, his sister Sanaa Seif said.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/request-accepted-egypt-lifts-travel-ban-on-activist-alaa-abdel-fattah-played-key-role-in-2011-uprising/articleshow/126095771.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/request-accepted-egypt-lifts-travel-ban-on-activist-alaa-abdel-fattah-played-key-role-in-2011-uprising/articleshow/126095771.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2025-12-20T22:18:42+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126095801,imgsize-83364.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[“Absolutely disgusting”: Asmongold backs Tylil James amid assault allegations and escalating online fallout with Jourdin Pauline]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126095051.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Asmongold publicly supported streamer Tylil James after he denied se*ual assault allegations made by Jourdin Pauline, calling her claims “disgusting” and suggesting she should face jail time for alleged extortion. Pauline fired back on X, standing by her accusations and saying police are involved. James has not responded to her latest posts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/absolutely-disgusting-asmongold-backs-tylil-james-amid-assault-allegations-and-escalating-online-fallout-with-jourdin-pauline/articleshow/126095051.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/absolutely-disgusting-asmongold-backs-tylil-james-amid-assault-allegations-and-escalating-online-fallout-with-jourdin-pauline/articleshow/126095051.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2025-12-20T20:58:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126095138,imgsize-64664.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How Russiagate ruined Cambridge scholar Svetlana Lokhova’s life]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126095252.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Cambridge historian, Svetlana Lokhova, found her life shattered by baseless Russian spy allegations linked to Russiagate. Despite no involvement in US politics or intelligence, fabricated claims of an affair with Michael Flynn led to professional ruin and public ostracization. Declassified documents later confirmed the allegations were recorded internally with doubts about their credibility, yet no accountability followed.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/how-russiagate-ruined-cambridge-scholar-svetlana-lokhovas-life/articleshow/126095252.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/how-russiagate-ruined-cambridge-scholar-svetlana-lokhovas-life/articleshow/126095252.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2025-12-20T21:33:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126095374,imgsize-44616.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Disturbing Epstein files photo of former Prince Andrew was taken inside the Royal family’s most treasured room]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126094637.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Newly unsealed Epstein files spotlight Prince Andrew with a resurfaced photo showing him with women and Ghislaine Maxwell at Sandringham Palace. The image's setting in a private royal gathering space intensifies scrutiny. Historian claims suggest the Queen was aware of past alleged misconduct at Buckingham Palace, which was reportedly covered up.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/disturbing-epstein-files-photo-of-former-prince-andrew-was-taken-inside-the-royal-familys-most-treasured-room/articleshow/126094637.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/disturbing-epstein-files-photo-of-former-prince-andrew-was-taken-inside-the-royal-familys-most-treasured-room/articleshow/126094637.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2025-12-20T20:45:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126094724,imgsize-24640.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['This is New Zealand, not India': Christian group performing haka confronts Sikh parade in Auckland — video]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126094759.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/this-is-new-zealand-not-india-christian-group-performing-haka-confronts-sikh-parade-in-auckland-video/articleshow/126094759.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/this-is-new-zealand-not-india-christian-group-performing-haka-confronts-sikh-parade-in-auckland-video/articleshow/126094759.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2025-12-20T21:31:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126094759,imgsize-923172.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bangladeshi national Zahid Hasan indicted for running three fake ID websites, earned $2.9 million; faces up to 125 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126094333.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/bangladeshi-national-zahid-hasan-indicted-for-running-three-fake-id-websites-earned-2-9-million-faces-up-to-125-years/articleshow/126094333.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/bangladeshi-national-zahid-hasan-indicted-for-running-three-fake-id-websites-earned-2-9-million-faces-up-to-125-years/articleshow/126094333.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2025-12-20T20:15:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-126094333,imgsize-1047324.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['No embargo': Pakistan refutes visit restrictions on Imran Khan's sons; promises visa approval]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/126094598.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Pakistan's government has denied any restrictions on former PM Imran Khan's sons visiting him in jail, assuring visas will be granted. This follows concerns raised by his sons, who fear they may never see their father again due to alleged isolation and harsh prison conditions. Officials refuted claims of solitary confinement and solitary confinement.]]></d